+ GlobalKind is U8

` How a module keeps a global. A constant's value is a literal, stored before any module
` starts. An eager one takes its value when its module starts, and a lazy one when it is
` first read. One each task holds its own of is `global-task`, kept in the memory of each
` task, and one each thread holds its own of `global-thread`, in the memory of each thread.
` One `do with` binds is `global-stack`, a slot in the memory of each task that says whether
` it is bound and holds its value. A value of an enum is made
` when its module starts, before the module's eager globals, where an emitted function reads
` it; one nothing emitted reads is `global-enum-unread`, and is not made.

| global-none = 0
| global-constant = 1
| global-eager = 2
| global-lazy = 3
| global-other = 4
| global-enum = 5
| global-enum-unread = 6
| global-task = 7
| global-thread = 8
| global-stack = 9

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
