━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ Witness is Struct

` The witness table of a type for an interface. `symbol` names the constant, and `slot` is
` the place the table of a class holds its address in, for a type that is a class.

+ value TypeId
+ interface TypeId
+ symbol StringId
+ slot U32 = no-slot-index

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ WitnessFunction is Struct

` The function a slot of a witness table holds for a type that declares its own answer to
` a function of the interface: it is given the interface value and calls `callee` with
` what the value holds, or with no callee reads the property at `property` of it. Where
` the type answers through a property it delegates to, `through` names the properties
` read from what the value holds to what `callee` takes. `converts` says `callee` takes an
` argument as another type than the interface's gives, as the type pass recorded. A `shared`
` one fills the slot in the table of each class that answers with `callee` itself, and
` `value` is the first of them.

+ value TypeId
+ proto InstanceId
+ callee InstanceId
+ property U32
+ through RowRange'U32
+ function FunctionId = no-function
+ converts Bool = false
+ shared = false

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ ClassAdapter is Struct

` The function a slot of a class's table holds for an override that answers another type
` than `proto`, the function the slot was made for: it calls `override` and converts what
` that answers to what `proto` answers.

+ proto InstanceId
+ override InstanceId
+ function FunctionId = no-function

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ GlobalStorage is Struct

` Where the program keeps a global, or the value of a parameter's default that runs code.
` `symbol` names its memory, which `layout` holds a value of `type` in. `state` names a byte
` beside a global that is not a constant: 0 while it has no value, 1 once it has, and 2 while
` a lazy one is being evaluated. `function` evaluates a lazy global that some emitted
` function reads. A default is kept for `owner`, the instance whose parameter it is: `syntax`
` is the default written, and `next` the default its module evaluates after it. A default a
` call evaluates has no memory: `function` evaluates it, and no module's list holds it. A
` global each task holds its own of is kept at `offset` in the memory of the task running,
` which has no symbol: `function` stores its value there, and `next` is the one of its module
` stored after it. One each thread holds its own of is `per-thread`, kept in the memory of
` the thread.

+ module ModuleId
+ decl DeclId
+ syntax SyntaxId
+ owner InstanceId
+ symbol StringId
+ state StringId
+ type TypeId
+ layout LayoutId
+ function FunctionId
+ next U32
+ offset U32 = U32.max
+ per-thread Bool

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ PropertyDefault is Struct

` The value a class gives a property its constructor is given none for: the module it is
` written in, the value, the declaration its conversion is recorded at, and that declaration
` among its module's. A property no class gives a value has value 0.

+ module ModuleId
+ value SyntaxId
+ site SyntaxId
+ decl DeclId

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ PlacedStyle is Struct

` A style or a style sheet some instance uses, numbered by its place among them, as the program
` registers it: `type`, `singleton` and the `count` rows from `first` are its `StyleUse`'s or its
` `StyleSheetUse`'s. `registered` says a function the program reaches uses it, and `module` and
` `site` are then where its registration is placed (`keep-reached-styles`).

+ type TypeId
+ module ModuleId
+ site SyntaxId
+ singleton InstanceId
+ first U32
+ count U32
+ registered Bool

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ ProgramTables
    is Usable'Void

` What emission reads about the whole program, built once after the seal: the functions the object
` holds, in the order it holds them, with their names; the layouts of its types, and of the unions
` tables hold rows of; the tables of its classes; the runtime's symbols; and the backend's manifest,
` whose string pool is whole before any worker runs. `instance-functions` gives the function of each
` emitted instance, `main-instances` the main of each module, `c-symbols` the symbol of each C
` function an emitted function calls, `c-suspends` whether that function suspends the task,
` `c-described` the runtime's function that does the same to storage and takes what describes it,
` `table-symbols` the table of each constructed class, and `slots` the place of each instance a
` table holds. `rtti-symbols` gives the constant that holds a type's name, key and property table,
` for each type some value is the type of and each class with a table. `initializer-functions` gives the function
` that runs a constructor on an object already made, for each constructor some `super(…)` names.
` `lazy-slots` gives the slot a class's table holds the function of a lazy property in, by the
` property's place. `storage` holds where each global and each default that runs code is kept.
` `slot-functions` gives the scope of the function that declares a slot, `slot-homes` the scope
` whose environment holds a slot nested functions capture, `slot-fields` its place there,
` `slot-copied` whether a slot no environment holds is one tasks spawned in its own function copy
` where they are spawned, `scope-captures` how many a scope holds, `scope-links` whether a nested
` function written in a scope captures a local from further out, `instance-scopes` the scope an
` instance is the function of, and `environments` the layout of the environment its own scope has. A
` loop whose body declares a local that nested functions capture has an environment for each turn:
` `turn-scope` gives its scope and `turn-environment` the layout an instance has for it. In a
` function that yields, the environment of the turn being run is kept in a field of the function's
` own: `turn-place` gives the field. `adapters` are the functions closures and bindings run as
` values of function types. `witnesses` are the witness tables of the types converted to interfaces,
` `prototypes` the functions of interfaces called through a value, in the order of their slots
` (`order-prototypes`), and `witness-functions` what the slots hold for a type with a function of
` its own.
` `equality-functions` gives the function each witness table holds for equality, or none.
` `class-adapters` are the functions the tables of classes hold for overrides that answer another
` type than the functions they stand in for. `forward-functions` gives the function made for each
` member a union forwards, by its place among the facts of such members, `forward-needs` says one
` needs a function of its own, and `forward-numbers` gives the `N` of the name of the function
` placed at one. `slots` gives the slot of a prototype within the section of its interface.
` `body-functions` gives the function that holds the body of an instance that is a function of an
` interface run for a value of a type that is none; the instance's own function sees the value as
` the interface and calls it. It gives too the function that holds the body of a constructor that
` fills its object with its class's markup (`fills-apart`), which the constructor's own function
` calls before it fills the object. `step-functions` gives the function that holds the body of an
` instance that yields: the instance's own function, or the one `body-functions` gives, makes the
` generator, a value that runs the body a step at a time. `scope-steps` says a scope is that of such
` a function, whose environment keeps every local it declares and, after the link, the step it has
` reached. `gate-functions` gives the function that evaluates the conditions of each row of
` `style-gates` again, and `gate-layouts` what the action that runs it keeps: the object, then the
` number of the block it gates, then the state cell of each `when` of the row that is one.
` `cell-functions` gives the function that gives each row of `scope-cells` its value again, and
` `cell-layouts` what the action that runs it keeps: the object, then the cell. `kept-layouts` gives
` the environment each of `kept-instances`, a function that builds markup and keeps state cells of
` the one it is written in, is given: the environment that one had in force where it made it, then
` each cell kept. `slot-forward-functions` gives the function each row of `slot-forwards` gives in
` place of the builder it forwards, and `slot-forward-layouts` what it keeps: the builder's code and
` data, then each cell it holds. `author-functions` gives the function that declares the value of
` each row of `style-authors` again, and `author-layouts` what the action that runs it keeps: the
` object, the block, the layer and the order. `given-functions` gives the function that declares
` again the line `given-sites` of a style rule that reads a value an application of
` `given-applications` with `live-values` gives it, and `given-layouts` what the action that runs
` it keeps: those an author's keeps, then the receiver where the values are written.
` `static-value-functions` gives the function that
` evaluates each row of `style-static-values`. `machine-order` lists the rows of `machines` in the
` order of the ranks of their instances, the order code that visits each of them takes them in. A
` batch starts each root's task main in a task of
` its own: `batch-main` forks the first `batch-starts` runs, and `batch-finishes` gives the function
` that ends each root's case and forks the next. The runtime is given the files of the batch:
` `batch-control`, where the cases are marked as they start and finish, and `batch-output` and
` `batch-errors`, where they print; and for each root its case's id and the directory it runs in.

+ bundle Bundle
+ layouts Layouts
+ unions UnionTables
+ functions Table'EmittedFunction
+ style-uses List'PlacedStyle'ArenaBacking
+ style-sheet-uses List'PlacedStyle'ArenaBacking
+ calls IdList
+ runtime-symbols IdList
+ module-paths IdList
+ instance-functions CPointer'U32
+ initializer-functions CPointer'U32
+ body-functions CPointer'U32
+ step-functions CPointer'U32
+ main-instances CPointer'U32
+ c-symbols CPointer'U32
+ c-suspends CPointer'U8
+ c-described CPointer'U32
+ table-symbols CPointer'U32
+ rtti-symbols CPointer'U32
_ property-tables CPointer'U32
+ slots CPointer'U32
+ lazy-slots CPointer'U32
+ slot-functions CPointer'U32
